{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nbase=json.load(open('update6.json'))['experiment']\ndef chain(b): return {\\\"field\\\":\\\"scenario\\\",\\\"reference\\\":b+\\\".scenario\\\"}\nbase['previous_id']=\\\"425ee562e1dc40a2928df98330de575c-experiment\\\"\nbase['revision_reason']=\\\"The harness now also contains a third scenario for the same cause: the single-voter removal with Config.CheckQuorum enabled, so the receipt can measure how long the removed leader keeps answering reads and what happens after it steps down. The earlier scenarios and their comparisons are kept.\\\"\nbase['scope']={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Observe the removed-leader ReadIndex path in three configurations of the same removal: a single-voter remainder, a two-voter remainder, and a single-voter remainder with CheckQuorum enabled (where the current leader answers the removed leader's old-term heartbeat with its higher term).\\\",\n \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n  \\\"Scenarios in one process: voters {1,2} where the removal leaves {2}; voters {1,2,3} where the removal leaves {2,3}; and voters {1,2} with Config.CheckQuorum true on both nodes; ReadOnlySafe and StepDownOnRemoval false in all of them.\\\",\n  \\\"In each scenario node 1 is elected leader, the application proposes and applies the committed removal of node 1 on every node, the remaining voters then elect node 2 and commit one entry, and only then is the ReadIndex request delivered to node 1.\\\",\n  \\\"In the CheckQuorum scenario the observations are taken before and after the first heartbeat tick of the removed leader, so the receipt covers both the window in which the stale answer is issued and the state after the step-down.\\\"],\n \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Lease-based reads (ReadOnlyLeaseBased).\\\",\\\"PreVote together with CheckQuorum.\\\",\\\"Snapshot transfer and asynchronous storage writes.\\\"]}\nbase['prefix']=\\\"Scenario A (single-voter remainder): elect node 1 in {1,2}, apply the committed removal of node 1, elect node 2 in {2} and commit one proposal, deliver MsgReadIndex to node 1, deliver the same request to node 2, run three heartbeat intervals on node 1 and deliver a second MsgReadIndex to node 1. Scenario B (two-voter remainder): elect node 1 in {1,2,3}, apply the committed removal on all three nodes, elect node 2 in {2,3} and commit one proposal, deliver MsgReadIndex to node 1, then run three heartbeat intervals on node 1. Scenario C (single-voter remainder with CheckQuorum): as scenario A with Config.CheckQuorum true, but the read is delivered before the removed leader has contacted the new leader, then one heartbeat tick is delivered and the step-down is observed, then a further MsgReadIndex is delivered.\\\"\nbase['prerequisites']=base['prerequisites']+[\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"csetup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_setup\\\"},\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"cremoved\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_leader_removed\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[chain(\\\"csetup\\\")]},\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"cnewlead\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_new_leader_committed\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[chain(\\\"cremoved\\\")]},\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"cread\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_read_before_stepdown\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[chain(\\\"cnewlead\\\")]},\n {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"cstep\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_stepdown\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[chain(\\\"cread\\\")]},\n]\nbase['comparisons']=base['comparisons']+[\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_leader_removed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"csetup\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"singleton\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Scenario C premise: with CheckQuorum enabled the removal still leaves node 1 leading a configuration whose single voter is node 2, so the shortcut applies.\\\"},\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_new_leader_committed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"cremoved\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"actual_leader_ahead\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Scenario C premise: the new leader of {2} has committed an entry the removed leader's commit index does not cover.\\\"},\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_read_before_stepdown\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"cnewlead\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_index_at_least_other_committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n  \\\"antecedent\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"read_states\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Scenario C witness before the step-down: enabling CheckQuorum does not remove the stale answer - the removed leader still answers with index 2 below the committed index 4 of the actual leader.\\\"},\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_stepdown\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"cread\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"state\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"StateFollower\\\"},\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Scenario C mitigation: the current leader answers the removed leader's old-term heartbeat with its higher term, so the removed leader becomes a follower (lead None) after one heartbeat tick.\\\"},\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_stepdown\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"cread\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"ticks_until_stepdown\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Scenario C bound: the stale-answer window is at most the heartbeat interval - one tick was enough for the step-down in the exercised configuration.\\\"},\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"c_read_after_stepdown\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"scenario\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"cstep\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"new_read_states\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Scenario C after the step-down: the same request is no longer answered (it is dropped because the node has no leader), so the exposure is bounded by the step-down rather than repaired inside raft.\\\"},\n]\nu={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Measure the boundary of the removed-leader finding instead of leaving 'CheckQuorum bounds the window' as an unmeasured limitation: the harness now also runs the single-voter removal with Config.CheckQuorum enabled, taking observations before and after the first heartbeat tick after the new leader was elected. The comparison set keeps the single-voter and two-voter scenarios and adds the CheckQuorum scenario. No interpretation is added this turn; the account stays as recorded until this receipt exists.\\\",\n \\\"experiment\\\":base}\nopen('update8.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update8.json 2>&1 | tail -6\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
